    "name_suffix": "_2026",
    "teacher_markdown": "## Assessment Level — Teaching Tips\r\n\r\n- **Push for specificity.**  \r\n  If students write something vague like “I changed the colors,” prompt them to name the exact element they changed (e.g., buttons, headings, card spacing).\r\n\r\n- **Require connection to prompting.**  \r\n  Make sure students explain how they refined or clarified their prompt, not just what changed visually.\r\n\r\n- **Check for CSS understanding.**  \r\n  If students describe structural changes, redirect them to explain how CSS controlled styling (not HTML structure).\r\n\r\n- **Look for usability impact.**  \r\n  Ask: “How did this change make the page clearer, more readable, or more consistent with the brand?”"
  },
